Redirect the Mac's camera (MS-RDPECAM) with AVFoundation.

FreeRDP's camera channel has only Video4Linux and Android back ends; on macOS
the build stopped at "libv4l-dev required". This adds a "mac" subsystem
(channels/rdpecam/client/mac/camera_mac.m): it announces the Mac's cameras,
the system default first, as RDCamera_Device_<n>, offers their sizes up to
1920x1080 at up to 30 fps as MJPEG, and compresses each frame with
VideoToolbox's JPEG encoder. The camera turns on when the server starts the
stream and off when it stops it.

encoding.c configured an H.264 encoder for every stream, also for MJPEG passed
through as it is. Our FFmpeg has decoders only, so that failed and no stream
could start; the encoder is now set up only for H.264 output.

The client asks for the channel with /vc:rdpecam.

